The Rest Interval
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/signal_array]

FIXME(mundane): The crew sits around a flat patch of rock about ten meters from the tower, the kettle in the middle, you among them. Veran has the head of the circle, the teapot by his knee. Baret is beside him. Richard is across the rock, heavy in his seat. Chorik sits next to you, a little apart from the talk, his teacup in both hands. The circle is small enough that anything said carries without anyone raising a voice. The bell is silent. The crew has time on the clock until they go back to the work.
choices:

* Turn to the foreman = He has the head of the circle and the teapot. [requires !tag signal_array.met_veran]
    FIXME(mundane): You turn to Veran at the head of the circle. He tops up your cup from the pot by his knee.
    FIXME(mundane): Veran is in his mid-fifties. He has the weathered build of a career fieldworker. He has been doing Kesharat infrastructure work for thirty years, he says. He is the foreman of this crew and signs off completion. The bell on his belt is field-issue; clever clockwork.
    FIXME(mundane): He asks where you have come from. He listens. He volunteers the crew's own route in return: they came down from the previous site three days ago. He names the landmarks. He describes the river crossing, the salt-flat traverse, the long climb up the south slope of the mesa.
    FIXME(dread): He says they made it in three days. You carry road distances for a living, and the legs he just named do not add to three days. The river crossing, the salt-flat traverse, the climb up the south slope of the mesa, strung in that order, is the better part of a week's walking. Every landmark is real. Made the way he says he made it, in the time he gives, the journey cannot be done.
    +open "Veran"

* Chat with the young worker = He has just settled in with a fresh cup of tea. [requires !tag signal_array.met_baret]
    FIXME(mundane): You turn to Baret, beside Veran.
    FIXME(mundane): Baret is in his late twenties. His hands have the build of someone who grew up working stone. His tunic cuffs are rolled and the Reshîd clan band on his wrist is visible whenever he reaches for the kettle.
    FIXME(mundane): He talks about his family. His mother is well. His sisters are well. His nephew was born while he has been on the road. He was supposed to be home for the birth. He knows he is overdue. He says he will be home after this job. Just this one more.
    FIXME(dread): He says "just this one more" twice in five minutes. He hears himself say it the second time. He laughs at himself a little. He does not stop saying it.
    +open "Baret"

* Meet the heavier man = He is across the circle, his weight on the rock. [requires !tag signal_array.met_richard]
    FIXME(mundane): You turn to Richard across the rock. He tops up your tea from where he sits.
    FIXME(mundane): Richard is in his forties. He says he is a pig farmer from the rich grasslands near Aldgate. He has a prize pig at home. His brother is taking care of her in his absence.
    FIXME(mundane): He asks if you have been by his farm. He describes it: the road in, the gate, the pig pen by the barn. He wants news. He reckons it is about time for the harvest festival. He worries about his brother's husbandry. He does not think his brother feeds the pig appropriately.
    +open "Richard"

* Check in on the quiet one = He sits next to you, a little apart from the talk. [requires !tag signal_array.met_chorik]
    FIXME(mundane): You turn to Chorik beside you. The circle is small enough that the others stay in easy earshot, conversations carrying without anyone raising a voice.
    FIXME(mundane): Chorik is buttoned to the throat. His uniform is new, unstained, no wear on the elbows or knees. You ask him how he is. He answers in short sentences. He does not initiate. When you press for more he changes the subject.
    FIXME(dread): The other three patch his discomfort with on-his-behalf inventions, contributing across the rock. Veran says Chorik has been quiet since the last site, don't mind him. Baret says Chorik is just tired, aren't you Chorik? Richard says don't ask him about that, he doesn't like to talk about it. Chorik does not contradict or elaborate. He drinks his tea.
    +open "Chorik"

* Sit back and watch = Stay quiet and listen [requires !tag signal_array.observed]
    +open "Observe"

* Wait out the rest interval = Let the time pass; they will finish the work after.
    FIXME(mundane): You stay where you are. The crew finishes their tea. The dust shimmer settles back over the road, and after a while the bell on Veran's belt rings again, softer this time. The crew rises from the rest circle and returns to the housing at the base of the tower. Veran checks the cable connections. Chorik fits the top cross-piece. Richard takes a laminated activation card out of his pocket. Baret rolls up the bedroll mat and stows the tea kit. The work resumes.
    +open "Completion"

* Walk off the work site = Decide this is not your concern
    FIXME(mundane): You stand. You thank Veran for the tea. You step out of the rest circle and back onto the mesa road. The crew watches you go without rising. The bell on Veran's belt does not ring again before you are out of earshot.
    +flee_dungeon
